WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.920
Do you ever feel like a fire breathing&nbsp;
dragon&nbsp;after eating spicy food? Like your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:08.920
throat is burning and you're about to exhale&nbsp;
a hot column&nbsp;of flames? No? Just me? Makes me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:13.720
wonder how dragons could breathe fire in the first&nbsp;
place. There are a lot of ideas how they might,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:17.560
but my favorite is based on the real life&nbsp;
abilities of the Bombardier Beetle. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:22.360
beetle has one amazing defense mechanism to&nbsp;
protect itself from&nbsp;predators. If threatened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:28.160
it mixes a combination of hydrogen peroxide and&nbsp;
hydroquinones inside&nbsp;special chambers in its body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.160
creating a super- heated chemical reaction&nbsp;
that elevates to near boiling. Then this deadly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:38.160
mixture is explosively sprayed on the beetle's&nbsp;
attacker. So maybe that's how dragons did it.&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.400
We may&nbsp;never solve the mystery of fire breathing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.160
in&nbsp;Dragon lore unless nature&nbsp;
reveals it in real animals.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.840
Between you and me I wouldn't want to&nbsp;stick&nbsp;
my head your dragon's mouth to find out.

